{{/*
family: net-snmp
what: trap
transports: v2c, v3
reference: net-snmp manual pages: snmpd.conf(5) (trap2sink, trapsess), snmp.conf(5) (defCommunity, defSecurityName, defAuthType…), snmptrap(1)
verification: tested
*/}}
{{define "does"}}Makes snmpd send its traps to Woodshed (SNMP{{.Transport}}), and gives a test trap to send with snmptrap.{{end}}

{{define "parts"}}
@@part file /etc/snmp/snmpd.conf Add to the agent's configuration, then restart snmpd (sudo systemctl restart snmpd); it sends a trap when it starts
# Woodshed: send traps (SNMP{{.Transport}}).
{{if eq .Transport "v2c"}}trap2sink {{.NetSNMPAddr}} <COMMUNITY>
{{- else}}trapsess -v 3 -u {{.V3User}} -l authPriv -a {{.Auth.NetSNMP}} -A <AUTH-PASSPHRASE> -x {{.Priv.NetSNMP}} -X <PRIV-PASSPHRASE> {{.NetSNMPAddr}}{{end}}
@@part file ~/.snmp/snmp.conf For the test trap: snmptrap reads its {{if eq .Transport "v2c"}}community{{else}}user and passphrases{{end}} from this file, not the command line
{{if eq .Transport "v2c"}}defCommunity <COMMUNITY>
{{- else}}defSecurityName {{.V3User}}
defSecurityLevel authPriv
defAuthType {{.Auth.NetSNMP}}
defAuthPassphrase <AUTH-PASSPHRASE>
defPrivType {{.Priv.NetSNMP}}
defPrivPassphrase <PRIV-PASSPHRASE>{{end}}
@@part command - Send a test trap
snmptrap -v {{if eq .Transport "v2c"}}2c{{else}}3{{end}} {{.NetSNMPAddr}} '' 1.3.6.1.4.1.32473.1.0.1 1.3.6.1.4.1.32473.1.1.1.0 s "Test trap for Woodshed from $(hostname)"
{{end}}

{{define "notes"}}
{{if eq .Transport "v2c"}}<COMMUNITY> must be one Woodshed accepts: Settings → Listeners → SNMP traps lists the communities (an empty list accepts any).
{{else}}Add the same user in Woodshed first: Settings → SNMP → v3 users, name {{.V3User}}, {{.Auth.Label}} and {{.Priv.Label}}, with the same passphrases (at least 8 characters each).
{{end}}
{{- if .IsName}}net-snmp looks the name up as IPv4; write udp6:[address]:port to send over IPv6.
{{end}}
Keep snmpd.conf readable by root only, and ~/.snmp/snmp.conf by you only (chmod 600 ~/.snmp/snmp.conf): they hold the {{if eq .Transport "v2c"}}community{{else}}passphrases{{end}}.
The test trap's OID is under the documentation enterprise number (32473), so it can't be mistaken for a real alarm.
{{end}}

{{define "check"}}Search Events for type Traps: the trap snmpd sends at start (coldStart) and the test trap each appear once; `woodshed snmp status` counts them.{{end}}
